From: Command Governor <divmode@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] extensions/oracle: feature-detect optional host capabilities

pi-oracle 0.7.20 does not load on hosts that implement the pi extension
contract but export a smaller surface than the reference build (observed on
Prime Agent 0.9.1). Three independent breaks, all fixed here without changing
any behaviour on the reference build:

  1. lib/config.ts and lib/runtime.ts import CONFIG_DIR_NAME,
     ProjectTrustStore and hasTrustRequiringProjectResources as runtime
     values. A host that does not export them yields undefined, and
     WORKSPACE_ROOT_MARKERS reaches join(undefined, ...) during module
     evaluation, so the whole extension fails to load.

  2. index.ts branches on ctx.mode, which some hosts do not put on
     ExtensionContext at all. Undefined took the wrong branch twice: the
     poller started in non-interactive runs, and resources_discover never
     contributed the prompt templates, leaving /oracle unusable.

  3. index.ts and lib/poller.ts reach ctx.ui.theme behind a ctx.hasUI guard.
     A host can report hasUI === true in a non-interactive run while its
     theme is uninitialised, so the property access throws. Because the
     status refresh runs from an async lifecycle callback, that surfaces as
     an unhandled rejection and can take the host session process down.

All optional host capabilities now live behind extensions/oracle/lib/
host-compat.ts, which always prefers the host's own value and only falls
back when the host omits one. On the reference build every branch resolves
to the previously imported symbol, so behaviour is unchanged.

Verified against @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 0.80.9:
  npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json          -> exit 0
  npm run typecheck:worker-helpers           -> exit 0
  npm run check:oracle-extension             -> exit 0 (esbuild bundle ok)
  npm run sanity:oracle                      -> fails identically before and
    after this patch on a machine without zstd/agent-browser; no behavioural
    difference is attributable to the patch.

